bext is a multi-crate project. Most of it is MIT-licensed. A small number of
"product" crates are released under the Business Source License 1.1, which
automatically converts to MIT on a defined Change Date.

  MIT (default):
    Applies to every crate and package in this repository EXCEPT those listed
    below. The MIT text appears further down in this file.

  Business Source License 1.1:
    Applies to the following crates. Each crate ships its own LICENSE.md
    with the full BSL 1.1 text and parameters:

      Commercial engine (the core runtime — the crown jewels):
        - crates/bext-core     (routing, SSR, caching, flow engine)
        - crates/bext-plugin   (plugin orchestration and lifecycle)
        - crates/bext-v8       (V8 SSR eval engine)
        - crates/bext-server   (HTTP server runtime and vhost dispatcher)

      Commercial "product" crates (standalone sellable surface):
        - crates/bext-waf          (web application firewall)
        - crates/bext-tls          (TLS termination and ACME)
        - crates/bext-nginx-compat (nginx config parser, drop-in replacement)
        - crates/bext-nginx-shim   (nginx CLI translator)

    Change Date:    2030-04-11
    Change License: MIT License
    Additional Use Grant: production use is permitted, except that you may
    not offer the Licensed Work as a hosted or managed service that provides
    third parties with access to a substantial set of its features.

  Closed source:
    The following crates are NOT distributed under any public license and
    are not published to any registry. They remain the private property of
    the copyright holder:
      - crates/bext-license
      - crates/bext-keygen

